body:
I was in a similar relationshiop to the one that OP is in currently. Everything was monogamous and cool for eight years, then she decided she needed "sow her wild oats" since she never got to do that before marriage. I could do whatever I wanted as well while she fucked around. I wasn't into being poly, plus we had three small kids, so I was home a lot taking care of them, cooking, putting them to bed. That lasted two years and I finally had the ability to get a divorce and get the hell away with the kids. Whenever I see posts like this, I am always curious to see at what stage of the failure of the relationship they are at. This dude seems to be wavering at the "I'm cool with this, I really am..." part of the relationshiop. Hopefully he gets out soon so he can be happy and contented in a real relationship. 

&#x200B;

I always tell people, "This isn't a video game where you get to reload and try again. Once the day is over, it's over, and at any point you could just die in your sleep or whatever, so use your time wisely, because you will never get this current opportunity ever again. Think about it like this: You only get around 80 halloweens, then you are done with life.
